Don't bother with those "oLS. You're wearing your "oRef anyway, and if
you take that off on the Planes for a single turn, the RNG guarantees
that in that very turn you'll get hit by four separate lightning rays
which will shatter all your "oLS _and_ your /oW and /oD. And if, at this
stage of the game, you come across something which kills you and which
is not player stupidity, "oLS is likely to dump your newly reborn body
straight back into its clutches. "oLS are a red herring, mostly.

> 11 !oFH, 14 !oHoly Water, 4 ?oGD (and a forgotten spell
> for confusion) for portal finding in the planes,

I'd suggest, if possible, taking one or two more of these, just because
finding the shifting portal on Water can be a bitch. That's convenience,
though, not necessity.

> a 0:1 wand of wishing,  1:5 and 1:2 /oDeath,

I always take as many /oD as I can, just for Rodney and (two of!) the
Riders. This _should_ be enough, but if you get thrown downstairs in
Gehennom more than usual (and you're lawful, so you probably will), and
therefore see Rodney reappear more than usual, the more /oD the better.

Also, ?oCharge, as a backup.

> a few /oS and plenty of teleportation and digging,

/oS is mostly useless at this stage. /oD is going to be important at one
point.

?oTele are useful, too, for levelports. Remember that you can levelport
down to the bottom, then find Rodney's tower and levelport up inside,
and once you've killed him levelport down to the Square level again.
Saves quite some time at a critical moment.

> blessed unicorn horn, 24 K-rations, and the Orb of Fate.

24 rations is overkill, but for your first ascension, as long as it
doesn't ever make you burdened (and remember that the Invocation
Artifacts are heavy), overkill is good.

